id: rail_mux_aux
label: RAIL multiplexer aux (CLI and raw API)
package: zigbee
category: 802.15.4|Radio
quality: evaluation
description: >
  Auxiliary RAIL multiplexer hooks (rail-mux-aux CLI group, raw RX/TX helpers). Evaluation-quality
  (alpha-stage); selected automatically when rail_mux is used with CLI.

provides:
- name: rail_mux_aux

requires:
- name: zigbee_cli

include:
- path: platform/radio/mac/rail_mux
  file_list:
  - path: sl_rail_mux.h
  - path: sl_rail_mux_rename.h
  - path: sli_rail_mux_aux.h
- path: app/framework/include
  file_list:
  - path: sl_zigbee_rail_mux_aux_cli.h
  - path: sl_zigbee_rail_mux_aux_raw.h
- path: stack/internal/inc
  file_list:
  - path: sl_zigbee_rail_mux_aux_raw_internal_def.h
- path: stack/internal/src/ipc
  file_list:
  - path: sl_zigbee_rail_mux_aux_raw_ipc_command_messages.h
    condition:
    - zigbee_use_ipc
  - path: sl_zigbee_rail_mux_aux_raw_ipc_callback_events.h
    condition:
    - zigbee_use_ipc

source:
- path: platform/radio/mac/rail_mux/sli_rail_mux_aux.c
- path: app/framework/cli/rail_mux_aux_cli.c
  condition:
  - zigbee_cli
- path: stack/internal/src/baremetal/sl_zigbee_rail_mux_aux_raw_baremetal_wrapper.c
  unless:
  - zigbee_use_ipc
- path: stack/internal/src/baremetal/sl_zigbee_rail_mux_aux_raw_baremetal_callbacks.c
  unless:
  - zigbee_use_ipc
- path: stack/internal/src/ipc/sl_zigbee_rail_mux_aux_raw_ipc_command_messages.c
  condition:
  - zigbee_use_ipc
- path: stack/internal/src/ipc/sl_zigbee_rail_mux_aux_raw_ipc_callback_events.c
  condition:
  - zigbee_use_ipc


template_contribution:
- name: component_catalog
  value: rail_mux_aux
- name: cli_group
  value:
    name: rail-mux-aux
    help: RAIL multiplexer aux CLI (PAN, mux register/unregister, raw aux RX/TX helpers).
- name: cli_command
  value:
    group: rail-mux-aux
    name: try-register
    handler: sl_zigbee_cli_rail_mux_aux_try_register
    help: Last mux context via sl_zigbee_rail_mux_aux_register_protocol; distinct PAN + short 0xFFFF; sl_rail_config_events (RX path); sl_rail_start_rx. Aux PAN must differ from stack (e.g. 0xCAFE vs 0xBABE). Channel 0 uses stack channel. Prints aux_rx_listen:ok or aux_rx_listen:skipped.
    argument:
    - type: uint16
      help: Auxiliary 802.15.4 PAN for the mux context (must not equal stack PAN).
    - type: uint8
      help: 802.15.4 channel for sl_rail_start_rx (0 = current Zigbee channel).
- name: cli_command
  value:
    group: rail-mux-aux
    name: unregister-aux
    handler: sl_zigbee_cli_rail_mux_aux_unregister_aux
    help: sl_zigbee_rail_mux_aux_unregister_protocol; stops aux RX, restores slot_base 0 and ZB+OT FCS listen. Prints mux_aux_tear:0xXXXX.
- name: cli_command
  value:
    group: rail-mux-aux
    name: auxcount
    handler: sl_zigbee_cli_rail_mux_aux_rx_count
    help: Prints mux_aux N; SL_RAIL_RX_PACKET_READY_SUCCESS/CRC_ERROR frames copied+released for try-register aux handle (not Zigbee stack MAC).
- name: cli_command
  value:
    group: rail-mux-aux
    name: mac-rx-unicast
    handler: sl_zigbee_cli_rail_mux_aux_mac_rx_unicast
    help: Zigbee stack MAC_RX_UNICAST counter (sl_zigbee_read_counters); not aux try-register RAIL RX. Use rail-mux-aux auxcount for the latter.
- name: cli_command
  value:
    group: rail-mux-aux
    name: tx-fixed-psdu
    handler: sl_zigbee_cli_rail_mux_aux_tx_fixed_psdu
    help: Aux TX fixed PSDU to FIFO then start_tx or CSMA TX; arms one-shot raw RX dump and TX complete observer via the unified internal aux event callback. try-register first. Ch0=stack ch.
    argument:
    - type: uint8
      help: 802.15.4 channel (0 = current Zigbee channel).
    - type: uint8
      help: 1 = start_cca_csma_tx (802.15.4 CSMA), 0 = start_tx.
- name: cli_command
  value:
    group: rail-mux-aux
    name: aux-rx-callback-off
    handler: sl_zigbee_cli_rail_mux_aux_raw_rx_off
    help: Clears unified aux event observer so auxcount drain resumes (e.g. after tx-fixed-psdu).
- name: cli_command
  value:
    group: rail-mux-aux
    name: rxdc-phy-select-get
    handler: sl_zigbee_cli_rail_mux_aux_rxdc_phy_select_get
    help: Prints mux_rxdc_phy_select 0 (Standard/FCS+HDR) or 1 (DC/FCS+HDR) for MUX builds with RX duty cycling and FCS.
- name: cli_command
  value:
    group: rail-mux-aux
    name: rxdc-phy-select-set
    handler: sl_zigbee_cli_rail_mux_aux_rxdc_phy_select_set
    help: Set mux RXDC PHY profile for MUX FCS builds. 0 = Standard/FCS+HDR, 1 = DC/FCS+HDR. Prints mux_rxdc_phy_select after update.
    argument:
    - type: uint8
      help: 0 = Standard/FCS+HDR, 1 = DC/FCS+HDR.

metadata:
  sbom:
    license: MSLA
root_path: zigbee
